.TH HD-REBOOT-CHECK 1 "October 2026" "hd-base" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-reboot-check \- tell whether the system needs a reboot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-reboot-check
.RB [ \-\-write ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-reboot-check
prints why the system needs a reboot to run what was installed, one reason
per line, or nothing when it does not:
.IP \(bu 4
the newest kernel in
.I /boot
is not the one running;
.IP \(bu 4
the ZFS module for the running kernel is not the one loaded, as after an
upgrade of
.BR zfs-dkms .
.PP
When neither is the case but
.I /run/reboot-required
exists, where Debian packages ask for a reboot, the packages in
.I /run/reboot-required.pkgs
that asked are the reason.
.PP
.BR hd-up (1)
runs it with
.B \-\-write
after an upgrade, and so does the kernel hook
.I /etc/kernel/postinst.d/zz\-hd\-reboot\-check
after a kernel is installed. The message after a login shows the reasons,
.BR hd-report (8)
sends whether a reboot is due to the dashboard, and hd-desktop shows a
notification in the desktop session. The system is never rebooted on its
own. The files are in
.IR /run ,
so they are gone after the reboot.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-write
When a reboot is needed, also write
.I /run/reboot-required
and add the packages that are not in
.I /run/reboot-required.pkgs
yet. Needs root.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, also when a reboot is needed; 1 when a file cannot be written.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/reboot-required
.TQ
.I /run/reboot-required.pkgs
A reboot is due, and the packages that need it.
.TP
.I /etc/kernel/postinst.d/zz\-hd\-reboot\-check
Runs
.B hd-reboot-check \-\-write
after a kernel is installed, outside a chroot, a conffile.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-base (7),
.BR hd-up (1),
.BR hd-reboot (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
